@startuml
' Four measured service times against the request timeout and the retry budget that
' were meant to bound them. Every measurement lies above the old request bound, so
' every attempt died at 20s: the operation was not slow, it was impossible.
'
' Notes for whoever edits this. (1) This PlantUML build's timing diagrams accept
' `caption`, `legend` and `highlight`, but reject multi-line note blocks and the
' `A@t1 <-> A@t2 : label` duration constraint, so the measurements are carried in the
' lane names and the commentary in the caption. (2) The axis draws one tick per time
' unit, so the window is kept to 70s: running it to B=150 renders 151 unreadable
' tick labels. The 150s budget is stated in the lane name instead.
title Measured service time against the bounds meant to hold it\n<size:11>a request can succeed only when <latex>\tau > \tau_{obs}</latex>, and a retry budget is honest only when <latex>B \geq 2\tau</latex></size>

scale 1 as 16 pixels

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam shadowing false

robust "listVersions #1\n<size:10>7 agents, 5 KB — 23.5 s</size>" as R1
robust "listVersions #2\n<size:10>same team, re-run — 30.5 s</size>" as R2
robust "listVersions #3\n<size:10>same team, re-run — 33.6 s</size>" as R3
robust "GET …/published\n<size:10>the call quoted in §9 — 25.4 s</size>" as R4
concise "BEFORE\n<size:10>20 s request bound,</size>\n<size:10>45 s budget</size>" as OLD
concise "AFTER\n<size:10>60 s request bound,</size>\n<size:10>150 s budget</size>" as NEW

highlight 0 to 20 #E1F5FE;line:0288D1
highlight 20 to 60 #FFEBEE;line:C62828 : where every measurement actually landed

@0
R1 is "evaluating" #FFF3E0
R2 is "evaluating" #FFF3E0
R3 is "evaluating" #FFF3E0
R4 is "evaluating" #FFF3E0
OLD is "attempt 1" #FFCDD2
NEW is "attempt 1" #C8E6C9

@20
OLD is "attempt 2" #FFCDD2

@23.5
R1 is "answered" #C8E6C9

@25.4
R4 is "answered" #C8E6C9

@30.5
R2 is "answered" #C8E6C9

@33.6
R3 is "answered" #C8E6C9
NEW is "all four answered" #ECEFF1

@40
OLD is "budget spent" #EF9A9A

@45
OLD is "500 — read timed out" #E57373

' Closing every lane at 60 s -- the new request bound -- so the axis covers the whole
' band the old configuration could not reach. `{hidden}` rather than a repeat of each
' lane's current state: repeating it makes PlantUML draw that state's name *past* the
' final tick, where the viewport clips it.
@60
OLD is {hidden}
NEW is {hidden}
R1 is {hidden}
R2 is {hidden}
R3 is {hidden}
R4 is {hidden}

caption <size:12>Both conditions failed at once, which is why a healthy node read as a broken one. Every measurement exceeds the 20 s request bound, so no attempt</size>\n<size:12>could finish; and a 45 s budget cannot hold two 20 s attempts plus retry overhead, so it ended the operation part-way through a second attempt that was</size>\n<size:12>equally doomed. The caller received one 500, with no way to distinguish "the node is unreachable" from "the node needed 24 s and was allowed 20".</size>\n<size:12>The bounds are now <latex>\tau = 60</latex> s under <latex>B = 150</latex> s, and the test asserts the relationship <latex>B \geq 2\tau</latex> rather than either constant — it was the relationship that broke.</size>

legend right
  |= colour |= meaning |
  |<#FFF3E0>| request in flight |
  |<#C8E6C9>| answered |
  |<#FFCDD2>| attempt that cannot succeed |
  |<#E57373>| operation reported as failed |
  |<#E1F5FE>| within the old request bound |
  |<#FFEBEE>| beyond the old bound, within the new |
endlegend
@enduml
